── General
?        help                                                       
q        close, or quit at the root                                 
esc      back out one level                                         
ctrl+c   cancel the running command, else quit                      
── Move
gg       top                                                        
G        bottom                                                     
j/down   down a line                                                
k/up     up a line                                                  
ctrl+d   half a page down                                           
ctrl+u   half a page up                                             
gt       jump to trunk()                                            jj log -r 'trunk()'
@        jump to the working copy                                   
── Picking
enter    run it                                                     
p        show the graph before / after the command                  
── Flags
-B       allow moving it backwards or sideways (--allow-backwards)  jj bookmark set --allow-backwards
